ue KC: Discordant trends in microvascular complications in adolescents with type 1 diabetes from 1990 to 2002. <source>Diabetes Care</source> <volume>28</volume>:<fpage>1974</fpage>&#x02013;1980, <year>2005</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16043741</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r12"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal">Donaghue KC, Fung AT, Hing S, Fairchild J, King J, Chan A, Howard NJ, Silink M: The effect of prepubertal diabetes duration on diabetes: microvascular complications in early and late adolescence. <source>Diabetes Care</source> <volume>20</volume>:<fpage>77</fpage>&#x02013;80, <year>1997</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9028699</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r13"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal">Eppens MC, Craig ME, Cusumano J, Hing S, Chan AK, Howard NJ, Silink M, Donaghue KC: Prevalence of diabetes complications in adolescents with type 2 compared with type 1 diabetes. <source>Diabetes Care</source> <volume>29</volume>:<fpage>1300</fpage>&#x02013;1306, <year>2006</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16732012</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r14"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal">Donaghue KC, Fairchild JM, Craig ME, Chan AK, Hing S, Cutler LR, Howard NJ, Silink M: Do all prepubertal years of diabetes duration contribute equally to diabetes complications? <source>Diabetes Care</source> <volume>26</volume>:<fpage>1224</fpage>&#x02013;1229, <year>2003</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12663601</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r15"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal">Stone ML, Craig ME, Chan AK, Lee JW, Verge CF, Donaghue KC: Natural history and risk factors for microalbuminuria in adolescents with type 1 diabetes: a longitudinal study. <source>Diabetes Care</source> <volume>29</volume>:<fpage>2072</fpage>&#x02013;2077, <year>2006</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16936155</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r16"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal">Wong TY, Knudtson MD, Klein 